SC5c instrumentation patch for rl_games/rl_games/common/a2c_common.py
======================================================================
This patch adds ONLY diagnostics (no algorithm change). It closes the SC5c
false-pass holes by logging, every epoch, the quantities the verdict script
cross-checks:

  gpu_level/active          float(self.gpu_level_sapg)              -- mechanism engaged?
  gpu_level/gather_calls    1.0 each epoch the gather branch ran    -- gather actually fired?
  gpu_level/num_blocks      self.num_actors//self.intr_coef_block_size in GLOBAL context
                                                                    -- == world_size, not 1 (no-op guard)
  perf/curr_frames          self.curr_frames * world_size           -- env-steps/epoch match precondition
  perf/num_minibatches      len(self.dataset)                       -- SGD work context for the FPS ratio
  perf/local_dataset_len    trained transitions on THIS rank        -- shard-size honesty (bound trained data)
  auxiliary_stats/off_policy_frac  fraction of off_policy_mask True -- followers relabelled (lf) engaged?

Peak memory is written to plain files at run end (max over the steady window),
BOTH allocated AND reserved, from the SAME torch API on cuda:local_rank:

  mem_<expname>_rank<R>.json  -> {"allocated": .., "reserved": .., "transient_allocated": ..}

`transient_allocated` is the peak *bracketed around the gather->shard window*
(reset at _gather_rollout entry, read just before _shard_batch) so the gpu-level
transient (the ws*local global batch + augment cat) is measured directly, not
inferred from the epoch-wide peak that other allocations may dominate.

The patch is idempotent-ish: all additions are guarded and byte-identical when
gpu_level_sapg is False EXCEPT for the extra scalar writes (rank-0 only) and the
mem file at exit -- these do not touch the RNG or the optimiser, so the A/B is fair.

Apply on the cluster dev pod from repo root:
    git apply tests/sc5c/sc5c_instrumentation.patch
Revert:
    git apply -R tests/sc5c/sc5c_instrumentation.patch

If you prefer NOT to patch source, run_sc5c.sh has an nvidia-smi sampler fallback
for memory (coarser, process-RSS-on-GPU) and the verdict script will detect the
absence of mem_*.json and fall back -- but then the correctness-coupled scalars
(gpu_level/*, perf/*) are UNAVAILABLE and SC5c MUST be reported INCONCLUSIVE, not
PASS, because the no-op / broken-impl holes cannot be closed without them.

