----------------------------------------------------------------------
Why experiment_name.split('_', 1)[1] and not [2:] or [3:]:
  - the CLI passes name=${RANK}_<base>. For rank>=10 the prefix is 3 chars, so a
    fixed [2:] would corrupt the filename. split('_',1)[1] strips exactly the
    "<rank>_" prefix for any rank width. (The rendezvous uses experiment_name[3:]
    at a2c_common:109 which ALSO breaks for single-digit ranks vs multi-digit but
    that is a pre-existing hash-seed quirk; we do NOT touch it -- our mem filename
    just needs to be stable per arm, and the verdict maps arm->rank explicitly.)
